{
  "title": "114: An-Naas الناس",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nقُلْ اَعُوْذُ بِرَبِّ النَّاسِۙ‏(1)\nQUL A-OO’ZO BE RABBIN NAASE.\nSay: ‘‘I seek refuge in the Lord of the people!\nمَلِكِ النَّاسِۙ‏(2)\nMALEKIN NAASE.\nThe King of the people!\nاِلٰهِ النَّاسِۙ‏(3)\nELAAHIN NAASE.\nThe God of the people!\nمِنْ شَرِّ الْوَسْوَاسِ  ۙ الْخَنَّاسِ ۙ‏(4)\nMIN SHARRIL WASWAASIL, KHANNAASIL.\nFrom the evil of the Satan (slinking whisperer,)\nالَّذِىْ يُوَسْوِسُ فِىْ صُدُوْرِ النَّاسِۙ‏(5)\nLAZEE YOWASWESO FEE SODOORIN NAASE.\nWho whispereth into the breasts (hearts) of the people\nمِنَ الْجِنَّةِ وَالنَّاسِ‏(6)\nMENAL JINNATE WAN NAAS.\nFrom among the Jinn and the Men",
  "merits": "This Surah was revealed in Madinah and it has 6 verse. Surah an-Naas and al-Falaq are together called Ma-o’ozatayn. Imam Ja’far as-Sadiq (a.s.) has said that whoever recites this Surah in his house every night, will be kept safe from Jinn and the evil designs of Shaitan.\nIf this Surah is put around the neck of a child as a talisman, the child will be protected from Jinn. Reciting the Ma-o’ozatayn before sleeping is a means of safety and if recited on any part of the body that is paining, the pain will be relieved."
}
